Subject: [PATCH 0017] Prism: native brand chrome elements (recon §5)

- Omnibox leading chip: LogiBricks mark + "Prism" pill at the left edge of
  the location bar (LocationBarView leading decorations, leftmost; the chip
  is pinned to ego's measured 22 DIP height, vertically centered).
- Top-right toolbar button: LogiBricks mark with a dark circular badge
  counting agent-controlled spaces (hidden at 0; 1s poll of SpaceManager,
  same source and cadence as the Dock badge). The badge is composited into
  the icon image (Button::OnPaint is final at this pin).
- Both open the shared Prism agent menu (focus an agent space's window /
  open the spaces overview / open the welcome page). The menu model+runner
  are owned by the invoking view because RunMenuAt is blocking on macOS.
- The mark is painted from the branding geometry (generate_icons.py), so it
  adapts to toolbar/omnibox theme colors; no raster assets needed.

All hunks anchor on pristine upstream lines (no stacking).

